While playing a neutral monk in my most recent game, I managed to
stumble into a polytrap while in the mines, on my way to the luckstone.
To my dismay, I ripped out of my robe and became a wyvern. I'd never
encountered wyverns as hostile mobs or otherwise, so I had no idea what
their capabilities were. However, after making short work of a horde of
fire ants, I figured that it might be in my best interests to go take
care of the cross-aligned altar while I was still morphed. I engaged
the priest, and slew him in three rounds without taking any damage. I
then went off to look for some sacrificial fodder. Happily, a black
unicorn teleported itself right in front of me. I destroyed it, grabbed
the corpse, and went over to the altar. I sacced it, figuring that my
hp of 106 would be enough to withstand whatever the soon-to-be-peeved
deity would throw at me. Unfortunately, I got the following messages.
[paraphrased from memory, of course.] The voice of Huan-ti booms out "
This action is an affront to Chaos!" You are fried by a bolt of
lightning! DYWYPI?

I'm not exactly sure what could have caused this, as I don't remember
the wrath of a god who's altar you are attempting to convert being
quite that dangerous. Perhaps wyverns are innately chaotic? If not
that, then it would have to be the fact that I was saccing a black
unicorn. Any information -as always- would be appreciated.

Incidentally, I had a shield of reflection, unequipped. Would that have
helped at all? I've never had reflection when dealing with wrath, so I
have no clue as to whether it makes a difference.



